# Primary Examples

## Scenario 1: How AI Makes Predictions

A 3rd-grade class uses a simple activity where students guess what word comes next in a sentence. The teacher then connects this to how AI predicts text based on patterns.

## Scenario 2: Checking AI Answers

A 4th-grade class asks an AI tool a question about animals. The teacher guides students to compare the response with a book or website to see if the information is accurate.

## Scenario 3: Exploring Bias in Examples

A 5th-grade class asks AI to generate examples of different jobs. Students notice patterns in how people are described and discuss whether everyone is represented fairly.

## Scenario 4: How AI Is Trained

A 2nd-grade class sorts pictures of objects (animals, food, tools) to simulate how AI learns from data. The teacher explains that AI learns by seeing many examples, just like they did.

## Scenario 5: Understanding AI Limits

A 5th-grade class asks AI a tricky or ambiguous question. When the answer is incomplete or incorrect, the class discusses why AI might not always get things right.
